            "heading": "",
            "text": "Environmental biotechnology careers use biological processes to treat wastewater, clean contaminated soil, convert waste to useful products and monitor ecosystems, and they reward people who combine microbiology, process control and regulatory understanding."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Learn microbiology and basic process engineering, spend time at a treatment plant or lab and document one small treatment trial."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Verify approvals and never join a venture that ignores them."
          }
